# Requests for every endpoint. Open in VS Code (REST Client) or Visual Studio / Rider.
# 1. Run "Sign in with password" and copy accessToken into @token below.
# 2. For MCP calls, create a personal access token and paste it into @pat.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5180
@token = paste-access-token-here
@pat = pat_paste-token-here
@postId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@designId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@groupId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@skillId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ---------- Public ----------

### Published posts (drafts never appear)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts

### One published post (404 for drafts and unknown slugs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/tenant-isolation-ef-core

### Projects
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects

### Figures a post can embed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/figures

### Contact form (5 per 10 minutes per IP, then 429)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/contact
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "kind": "role",
  "name": "Jane Recruiter",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "organization": "Example Ltd",
  "topic": "Senior .NET Developer",
  "message": "We would like to talk about a full-stack role.",
  "website": ""
}

### ---------- Auth ----------

### Sign in with password (dev admin from user-secrets)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@portfolio.test", "password": "see dotnet user-secrets list" }

### Sign in with Google (idToken = credential from the Google button)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json

{ "idToken": "eyJ..." }

### Refresh (uses the HttpOnly cookie set at sign-in)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh

### Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sign out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### ---------- Admin: posts ----------

### All posts incl. drafts
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a draft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Audit trail rows in the ERP",
  "excerpt": "How every change is recorded without slowing down the fee desk.",
  "body": "Intro paragraph.\n\n::layer{id=data}\n\n## The table\n\nText.",
  "category": "Architecture",
  "layer": "data",
  "tags": ["audit-trail", "ef-core"]
}

### Update
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Audit trail rows in the ERP",
  "excerpt": "Updated excerpt.",
  "body": "Updated body.",
  "category": "Architecture",
  "layer": "data",
  "tags": ["audit-trail"]
}

### Publish
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/posts/{{postId}}/publish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Unpublish
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/posts/{{postId}}/unpublish
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Admin: messages and tokens ----------

### Contact messages
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an MCP token (secret shown once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/api-tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Claude Desktop", "expiresInDays": 90 }

### List tokens
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/api-tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Design gallery (public) ----------

### Visible design items, gallery order (200 with [] until you upload some)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/design-posts

### One item's image as WebP (use the imageUrl from the list; cached 1 year, ETag gives 304)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/design-posts/{{designId}}/image

### ---------- Skills (public) ----------

### Skill cards with their skills, in order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/skills

### ---------- Admin: skills ----------

### All cards (same shape as the public list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/skills
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a card
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/skills/groups
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cloud and DevOps" }

### Rename a card
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/skills/groups/{{groupId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Cloud" }

### Add a skill to a card (icon: a key from SkillIcons.cs, or null)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/skills/groups/{{groupId}}/skills
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Docker", "level": 70, "icon": "docker", "note": null }

### Change a skill (add "groupId" to move it to another card)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/skills/{{skillId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Docker", "level": 75, "icon": "docker", "note": null }

### New card order (every card id once)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/skills/groups/order
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ids": ["{{groupId}}"] }

### Delete a skill
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/skills/{{skillId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a card and its skills
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/skills/groups/{{groupId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- CV ----------

### Is a CV available? (always 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cv/info

### Download the CV (404 when none is uploaded)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cv

### Admin: current CV details (204 when none)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/cv
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin: upload or replace the CV (PDF, up to 5 MB)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/cv
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=cv

--cv
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="cv.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./cv.pdf
--cv--

### Admin: remove the CV
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/cv
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Admin: dashboard overview ----------
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- Admin: design gallery ----------

### All items, hidden ones included
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/design-posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One item
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/design-posts/{{designId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Upload (multipart). The file is compressed to WebP, at most 100 KB, aspect ratio kept.
### Put a real image next to this file (here: sample.jpg) before running it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/design-posts
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=design

--design
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="caption"

Poster for a campus event
--design
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="link"

https://example.com/original-post
--design
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample.jpg
--design--

### Change caption, link and visibility
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/design-posts/{{designId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "caption": "Poster for a campus event", "link": null, "isVisible": true }

### Replace the image only (caption and position stay)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/design-posts/{{designId}}/image
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=design

--design
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./sample.jpg
--design--

### Save a new order: every item id once, first item first
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/design-posts/order
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ids": ["{{designId}}"] }

### Delete an item and its image
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/design-posts/{{designId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ---------- MCP (JSON-RPC over Streamable HTTP) ----------

### List tools
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{pat}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list" }

### Call a tool
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{pat}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "tools/call", "params": { "name": "list_posts", "arguments": {} } }
